## I-06: Exotic Device Support Research

### DualSense Controller (PS5)

| Feature | Linux Support | API |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| Buttons/Sticks | ✅ hid-playstation | evdev |
| Triggers (analog) | ✅ hid-playstation | evdev |
| Touchpad | ✅ hid-playstation | evdev |
| Gyro/Accel | ✅ hid-playstation | evdev |
| Rumble | ✅ hid-playstation | evdev FF |
| Player LEDs | ✅ hid-playstation | leds-class |
| Lightbar RGB | ✅ hid-playstation | leds-class-multicolor |
| **Adaptive Triggers** | ❌ Not in driver | hidraw only |
| **Advanced Haptics** | ❌ Not in driver | hidraw only |

### evdev Force Feedback Types

| Effect Type | Use Case | Supported by evdev |
|-------------|----------|-------------------|
| `FF_RUMBLE` | Strong/weak motor | ✅ |
| `FF_SPRING` | Return to center | ✅ |
| `FF_DAMPER` | Velocity resistance | ✅ |
| `FF_FRICTION` | Position resistance | ✅ |
| `FF_INERTIA` | Mass simulation | ✅ |
| `FF_CONSTANT` | Constant force | ✅ |
| `FF_PERIODIC` | Sine/triangle waves | ✅ |
| `FF_RAMP` | Linear force change | ✅ |

### Future hidraw Requirements

For adaptive triggers, RGB LEDs beyond leds-class, and VCM haptics:
- Direct hidraw access needed
- Custom packet structure per device
- Device-specific drivers in userspace

